The central limit theorem gives an approximately normal sampling distribution, with
$\begin{align*}\sigma_{\bar{X}}&=\frac{30}{\sqrt{100}}\\&=3\text{ g}.\end{align*}$
(a)
$\begin{align*}z&=\frac{206-200}{3}\\&=2.\\P(\bar{X}>206)&\approx P(Z>2)\\&\approx\frac{1-0.95}{2}\\&=0.025.\end{align*}$
