(b)
$\begin{align*}z&=\frac{197-200}{3}\\&=-1.\\P(\bar{X}>197)&\approx P(Z>-1)\\&\approx0.34+0.5\\&=0.84.\end{align*}$
The corresponding lower-tail probabilities are approximately $P(\bar{X}<206)=0.975$ and $P(\bar{X}<197)=0.16$.

The sampling distribution is approximately normal, with
$\begin{align*}\sigma_{\bar{X}}&=\frac{18}{\sqrt{81}}\\&=2.\end{align*}$
(a) The boundary $z$-scores are
$\begin{align*}z_{76}&=\frac{76-80}{2}=-2,\\z_{84}&=\frac{84-80}{2}=2.\\P(76<\bar{X}<84)&\approx P(-2<Z<2)\\&\approx0.95.\end{align*}$
(b) The lower boundary now has $z_{78}=\frac{78-80}{2}=-1$.
$\begin{align*}P(78<\bar{X}<84)&\approx P(-1<Z<2)\\&\approx0.34+0.475\\&=0.815.\end{align*}$
